r", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376333, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JFt2g13uriVKtbWvLisfd6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 380574, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. Because of this, `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the function to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on that commit (08d3cd5986) passed.\n- **PR:** #101 \u2014 https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval. When I tried to look up FIN-212, the advisory system said it doesn't exist. That didn't block the fix: both the test and the docstring already call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AgnT2Yb53UY6PsY1o8rRsy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Qp5xXnbx1QWYnCmzA4tx5r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PZ9MLc5EHrAWANCr1ion3L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu